  "notes": "Transcribed from the official SCC 'Biology AS-T Degree' program map, Catalog 2026-27, published May 27, 2026 (mapmaker.losrios.edu/Maps/7560/PublishedPdf). GE Pattern: Cal-GETC. Associate Degree for Transfer (ADT). Official Total Units: 61-62; this seed models the first-listed/recommended path = 15+16+15+15 = 61 units (ENGL C1000 at 3 units per the official SCC English course page). Semester sums verified against the map's 15-16 / 16 / 15 / 15 headers. In-plan prereqs per the map: BIOL 402 requires CHEM 400 with 'C' or better; CHEM 401 requires CHEM 400 with 'C' or better; BIOL 412 requires BIOL 402 (or equivalent college-level Cell and Molecular Biology) with 'C' or better; BIOL 422 requires BIOL 402 (or equivalent) with 'C' or better; PHYS 360 requires PHYS 350 with 'C' or better. Prior/placement prereqs (documented, not in prereq arrays): MATH 355 requires MATH 373 with 'C' or better or placement (students not placing directly may need the MATHS 65/MATH 355 combo; another equivalent Calculus course may substitute for MATH 355); CHEM 400 requires CHEM 300 with 'C' or better completed within one year prior to enrollment, or placement via the ACS California Chemistry Diagnostic Exam completed within one year, AND Intermediate Algebra or equivalent (Integrated Math 3) with 'C-' or better; PHYS 350 requires high school Trigonometry or equivalent or MATH 373 with 'C' or better. This path is designed for students who place into CHEM 400 by passing the Chemistry Diagnostic Exam and have MATH 355 placements — see an SCC counselor for planning. Advising notes: Cal-GETC Area 4 requires 2 courses from different disciplines — the Semester 4 Area 4 GE course must be from a different discipline than the Semester 3 Area 4 course; students not placing directly in ENGL C1000 take the ENGL 80/ENGL C1000 combo. ADT requirements: all major courses with 'C' or better; 60 CSU-transferable units (12 within Los Rios); Cal-GETC Areas 1-6 with 'C' or better. tccns mirrors SCC local course codes (California community colleges do not use TCCNS).",
